# Line-ending policy: LF everywhere, in the repository AND in the working tree.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Git for Windows ships with core.autocrlf=true, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. That silently breaks four gates in this repository, and it breaks
# them on the developer's machine only - CI on Linux stays green, so the
# failure looks like a merge problem when it is not:
#
#   constants-drift          compares a generated file against BANNER + source,
#   validate-taxonomy        where BANNER is a JS literal ending in '\n'. A
#   validate-study-planner   CRLF working tree makes every byte-identical
#                            comparison fail even though the content is right.
#
#   validate-ai-tutor-source is a bash script. With CRLF endings the shebang
#                            line and `set -o pipefail` fail outright:
#                            "$'\r': command not found".
#
# Those four are exactly the drift/parity gates that keep the generated copies
# (taxonomy.js, _shared/taxonomy.core.js, study-planner.js) honest, so losing
# them loses the guarantee that the Edge Function ships the same taxonomy the
# browser uses. The fix is to make LF normative rather than to loosen the
# comparisons - the files are byte-compared on purpose.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` means: detect text files, store them with LF, and check
# them out with LF on every platform including Windows. PowerShell 7, Node and
# Git Bash all read LF correctly, and there are no .bat/.cmd files here (those
# would genuinely require CRLF).
#
# AFTER PULLING THIS FILE for the first time on Windows, refresh the working
# tree once so existing CRLF files are rewritten:
#
#   git add --renormalize .
#   git checkout -- .

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets - never touch these.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
# Audio. The first audio in this repository; without these lines `text=auto`
# would sniff them as text and rewrite bytes on checkout.
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
*.ogg  binary
*.m4a  binary
